WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:06.020
From a terrifying Romanian abbey to a murderous
occultist in Connecticut, the story told through

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.329
the Conjuring movies spans decades.

00:00:08.329 --> 00:00:10.101
Here's how all the pieces fit together.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.000
Chronologically speaking, the Conjuring Universe
all starts with "The Nun."

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.015
Released in 2018, this film takes place in
1952, at the Abbey of St. Carta in Romania.

00:00:21.015 --> 00:00:25.920
Father Burke and a novitiate, Sister Irene,
have been dispatched by the Vatican to investigate

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.508
the suicide of one of the abbey's nuns.

00:00:28.508 --> 00:00:31.869
After a bit of research, they discover the
nuns have been spending most of their time

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:36.570
praying in shifts to keep a nun-shaped evil
entity from hitchhiking its way out into the

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:39.020
real world on a human host.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.910
As it turns out, the abbey was originally
built by a duke during the Middle Ages who

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:46.230
was more interested in demon worship than
Catholicism.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:50.140
He managed to raise the demon Valak but was
stopped by a group of Christian knights who

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:53.410
were able to seal Valak, at least temporarily.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:57.570
With the help of a nice local man named Frenchie,
Father Burke and Sister Irene finally banish

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:02.768
Valak back to Hell, thanks to an ancient artifact
filled with the blood of Jesus Christ.

00:01:02.768 --> 00:01:07.511
"You should have kept running when you had
the chance, Frenchman."

00:01:07.511 --> 00:01:09.911
"I'm French-Canadian."

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.376
Or, at least, they think they've beaten the
demon.

00:01:13.376 --> 00:01:19.295
But as it happens, Valak manages to hitch
a supernatural ride out of town on Frenchie's back.

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:23.600
The Valak character in the Conjuring Universe
may have taken its inspiration from a demon

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.860
with a slightly different name described in
Aleister Crowley's "The Lesser Key of Solomon"

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:31.397
as a "child with angel's wings riding on a
two-headed dragon."

00:01:31.397 --> 00:01:36.497
The Conjuring Universe version of Valak is
clearly not a child, and it doesn't have angel's wings.

00:01:36.578 --> 00:01:40.020
Whether or not it rides a two-headed dragon
is up for some debate, since who's to say

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.688
that the dragon didn't get left behind when
Valak crossed over from Hell.

00:01:43.688 --> 00:01:48.457
One very specific thing that's mentioned in
both mythologies, however, is their connection to snakes.

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:52.759
Like Crowley's demon, who's known "to tell
where serpents may be seen," the Valak of

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:57.409
the 1950s Romanian monastery has its own tie
to the biblical reptile, along with a much

00:01:57.409 --> 00:01:59.005
more impressive title:

00:01:59.005 --> 00:02:09.685
"The Defiler, the Profane, the Marquis of
Snakes."

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:14.280
As fans of the franchise know, Valak goes
on to become a major recurring villain in

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.340
the story of the Conjuring Universe.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:22.340
"The Nun II" picks up only a few years later
in 1956, as Sister Irene hides out in Italy

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.959
following her battle with Valak.

00:02:23.959 --> 00:02:28.660
But, after catching wind of a mysterious series
of deaths, not to mention an eerie vision

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:33.330
of a distressed Frenchie, the nun gets permission
to investigate these bizarre happenings.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:38.550
Sadly, Father Burke has passed away, but joining
Irene this time around is Sister Debra, a

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.120
nun who lacks faith.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.420
Of course, this all leads to Valak's triumphant
return.

00:02:43.844 --> 00:02:48.083
"What did you see?"

00:02:49.395 --> 00:02:51.637
"I saw a nun."

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.281
During Sister Irene's investigation, she learns
that Valak is after a Catholic relic, the

00:02:56.281 --> 00:03:01.000
eyes of Saint Lucy — a Christian martyr
who was supernaturally kept from burning alive,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.379
a quality her descendants share.

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:06.870
The eyes of Saint Lucy happen to be hidden
in the French boarding school where Frenchie

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.240
currently works.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.340
With the help of a young girl named Sophie,
Irene uncovers the relic, which the Valak-possessed

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.370
Frenchie takes for himself soon after.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:19.920
At full strength, Valak attempts but fails
to burn Irene alive, revealing that Irene

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.019
is a descendant of St. Lucy herself.

00:03:23.019 --> 00:03:28.019
After Sisters Irene and Debra pray fervently,
Valak is seemingly banished back to hell,

00:03:28.019 --> 00:03:29.730
and all seems well.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:34.709
Except it's not: the movie ends with a flash-forward
to Ed and Lorraine Warren receiving an interesting

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:41.090
call, likely teasing Frenchie's inevitable
re-possession, or maybe something even more sinister.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:45.840
The story of Annabelle the demon doll starts
in 1943 with "Annabelle: Creation," when a

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.319
dollmaker named Samuel Mullins and his wife
Esther lose their seven-year-old daughter,

00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:52.126
Annabelle, in a freak car accident.

00:03:52.126 --> 00:03:57.239
About 12 years later, in 1955, the Mullins
decide they've spent enough time without a

00:03:57.239 --> 00:04:01.180
child, so they open their doors to a group
of orphaned girls and the nun tasked with

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.780
their care, a woman by the name of Sister
Charlotte.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.650
When one of the orphans, a girl named Janice,
stumbles upon a porcelain doll in a locked

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:14.090
bedroom, she unwittingly releases a demon
that wreaks havoc on the house and its inhabitants.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:17.880
It's soon revealed that following their daughter's
death, the Mullins had been tricked into letting

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:22.030
a demon take possession of one of Samuel's
dolls, and it's now decided to try and find

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.590
a human host.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:28.220
By the end of the ordeal, the demon has succeeded
in possessing Janice, who escapes and — now

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:32.870
going by the name Annabelle — winds up being
adopted by a nice family in Santa Monica,

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:37.220
where she grows up, runs away, joins a cult,
and then returns to murder her adoptive parents

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.970
in 1967.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.073
Talk about a downbeat ending.

00:04:41.073 --> 00:04:48.874
"So, which one of you gets this?"

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:53.780
As it turns out, the nice family that adopted
Annabelle lives next door to John and Mia

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:57.090
Form, the main protagonists of 2014's "Annabelle."

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:02.070
John has given his wife Mia an antique porcelain
doll as a gift for their unborn child.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:06.949
But after Janice-slash-Annabelle and her boyfriend
kill her parents, they move on to the Form

00:05:06.949 --> 00:05:11.370
residence, where Annabelle takes a sudden
and deadly liking to Mia's antique.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.458
"I like your dolls."

00:05:14.458 --> 00:05:19.657
During the struggle, she takes her own life
and transfers the demon back into its original home.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:24.250
Terror sets in as the demon doll decides that
Mia would make a nice soul sacrifice.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.970
The couple is helped by a local bookseller
named Evelyn and their parish priest, Father

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:31.850
Perez, the latter of whom tries to take the
doll to Ed and Lorraine Warren, but is attacked

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.889
before he has the chance.

00:05:33.889 --> 00:05:38.070
Willing to sacrifice her own soul to save
her newborn daughter, Mia tries to jump out

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.760
of her window with the doll.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:43.956
Luckily, John and Evelyn arrive in time to
stop her, and Evelyn takes the doll ... and

00:05:43.956 --> 00:05:45.740
Mia's place.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:48.257
"There has to be another way."

00:05:48.257 --> 00:05:49.326
"There is.

00:05:50.094 --> 00:05:51.987
I can make it right."

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:56.389
In the end, an unsuspecting woman buys the
doll from a toyshop as a gift for her daughter,

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:57.428
a nurse.

00:05:57.428 --> 00:06:02.978
Here's where we finally get our first proper
introduction to Ed and Lorraine Warren in 1968.

00:06:02.978 --> 00:06:07.669
That nurse, whose mother had given her a very
hideous doll as a present, is now at the mercy

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:12.370
of the demon spirit trapped inside the toy,
and she needs the Warrens' help in exorcizing

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:13.370
the thing.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:17.946
So the Warrens take the doll off the nurse's
hands and move on to their next case.

00:06:17.946 --> 00:06:24.707
In 1971 in Wakefield, the Warrens are teaching
a class on demonology at Massachusetts Western University.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:29.319
One of the attendees at the Warrens' demonology
lecture is Carolyn Perron, a wife and mother

00:06:29.319 --> 00:06:32.740
whose family has recently moved into a Rhode
Island farmhouse.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:37.620
And unfortunately, they're now being tormented
by a malevolent, clap-happy spirit.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:47.250
"Give me the third clap."

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.310
But it's not all fun and games when it comes
to this hellspawn.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:53.979
After some digging, the Warrens discover the
house was built on land that once belonged

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:58.480
to a witch named Bathsheba, who sacrificed
her week-old child to the devil before hanging

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:03.270
herself, and then spent the following century
possessing and killing future residents.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:07.150
Ed and Lorraine suggest the family move into
a motel temporarily, while they try to get

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.870
the Catholic Church to agree to an exorcism.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:13.729
But Bathsheba has already set her sights on
Carolyn, and the now-possessed mother brings

00:07:13.729 --> 00:07:16.250
her kids back to the house to kill them.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:20.570
The Warrens show up in time for Ed to perform
a rogue exorcism on his own, and the curse

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:25.090
of Bathsheba is lifted, leaving the Perrons
with a livable farmhouse and the Warrens free

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.750
to move on to a new case.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:33.330
A year after all that, in 1972, When Ed and
Lorraine Warren are needed on an overnight

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:37.870
investigation, they hire a teenager named
Mary Ellen to babysit their daughter Judy.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.479
This turns out to be a terrible decision.

00:07:40.479 --> 00:07:44.990
Not only do the Warrens at this point in time
have an entire room devoted to possessed objects

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:49.720
in their home, but Mary Ellen has a friend
named Daniela who really wants to speak to

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:50.940
her dead father.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:55.470
Daniela drops by the house uninvited and does
what any girl in her position would do.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:59.849
She finds a way into the Warrens' artifact
room, disturbs Annabelle, and unleashes every

00:07:59.849 --> 00:08:03.110
ghost and demon the Warrens have trapped in
their basement.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:05.750
"It's the doll, Ed.

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:10.270
It's a beacon for other spirits."

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:14.419
Understanding that, the three girls set about
trying to get the doll back in her glass prison,

00:08:14.419 --> 00:08:16.650
hoping that will stop the haunting.

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:20.400
The girls spend the night essentially playing
hide and seek with a bunch of possessed objects

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:25.000
before Annabelle is returned to her case once
and for all.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:29.819
Valak makes its return in 2016's "The Conjuring
2," the film that sees Ed and Lorraine Warren

00:08:29.819 --> 00:08:33.070
finally defeat the Marquis of Snakes…maybe.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:37.750
Beginning in 1976, the couple is investigating
the infamous Amityville murders, and Lorraine

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:41.620
has a vision where one of the murdered DeFeo
children leads her to the basement, and she

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.540
comes face to face with Valak and a vision
of her husband's death.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:50.350
Lorraine continues to see visions of the demon
nun, even as the pair travel to Enfield, England,

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:54.120
where the Hodgson family has been experiencing
paranormal activity.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.570
When it appears as though the entire haunting
is a hoax put on by the family to gain fame,

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:00.980
the Warrens pack up their things to leave.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:05.560
But Lorraine soon realizes that Valak has
been behind the entire thing, and they return

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:09.720
to the house in a last ditch effort to save
the eldest daughter, Janet, who at this point

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:12.470
is possessed and trying to jump out a window.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:16.769
Ed grabs her, but almost falls to his death
in the process, leaving Lorraine to go head

00:09:16.769 --> 00:09:18.829
to head with Valak herself.

00:09:18.829 --> 00:09:22.960
She succeeds in banishing the demon by using
its name and pulls Ed to safety.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:28.870
"I condemn you back to heeeeeell."

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:30.420
Close call!

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:36.870
A few years later, in 1981, the Warrens document
the exorcism of a young boy named David Glatzel.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:41.510
Unfortunately, the evil spirit in David overpowers
Ed and makes a deal with Arne Johnson, the

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.580
young man dating David's older sister Debbie.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:48.079
Arne offers himself up in David's place, and
the demon accepts.

00:09:48.079 --> 00:09:52.709
Though Ed sees this happen, he loses consciousness
for over a month, giving the demon-possessed

00:09:52.709 --> 00:09:55.480
Arne just enough time to murder his landlord.

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:59.890
Eventually, Ed and Lorraine learn that David
was possessed only after first being cursed

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:02.990
by an object built by Isla the Occultist.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:06.890
This leads them to Father Kastner, a retired
priest who has previously dealt with a cult

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.893
called the Disciples of the Ram.

00:10:08.893 --> 00:10:14.990
It turns out that he's also the secret father
of Isla, who he accidentally exposed to occult practices.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:19.020
To save Arne, the Warrens destroy the altar
that Isla built, expelling the demon before

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:20.680
it can do any more damage.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:24.970
Unfortunately for Isla, the demon returns
to its former master, killing the Occultist

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.100
and dragging her soul to Hell.

00:10:27.302 --> 00:10:29.882
Ed and Lorraine's story isn't done just yet.

00:10:29.882 --> 00:10:34.260
A fourth "Conjuring" film, titled "The Conjuring:
Last Rites," is currently in development,

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:39.260
with Patrick Wilson and Vera Farmiga returning
as everyone's favorite paranormal investigators.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:43.529
Produced once more by James Wan and Peter
Safran, "Last Rites" looks like it could potentially

00:10:43.529 --> 00:10:46.628
be Ed and Lorraine's final Conjuring Universe
adventure.

00:10:46.628 --> 00:10:51.278
No matter how it plays out, it'll be great
to see them tackle the forces of evil yet again.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.040
Additionally, a Conjuring Universe TV series
is also in the works at Max, which may be

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:01.270
another spooky avenue for the Warrens' most
hideous adversaries to rear their ugly heads.

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:05.020
Given how early in development the series
is, we don't have many details.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:07.840
In fact, you could say we have nun.

